.nh
.TH "PVEFORGE" "1" "Sep 2026" "pveforge" "pveforge manual"

.SH NAME
pveforge-harness-probe - Probe an outer storage's capability (creates and destroys VM 690)


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpveforge harness probe <target-id> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Probe an outer storage's capability for the harness, on VM 690, before the
build. The static layer checks the storage is an enabled, active zfspool that
holds images and has room; the empirical layer creates a 1 GiB disk VM,
snapshots it, classifies the storage's rollback rule (rollback-latest-only vs
rollback-any), then destroys 690 and proves it gone. --static-only runs the
static layer alone. The rollback rule is written to
~/.config/pveforge/harness-state/rollback-rule.<id> (a probe output; reset
does not read it).


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--created-file\fP=""
	path to this run's created-VM ledger (default $HARNESS_CREATED_FILE)

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for probe

.PP
\fB--lock-wait\fP=0s
	how long to wait for another pveforge process's lock on this object before giving up (0 = the 15m0s default; at most 1h0m0s). The default exceeds the 10m0s ceiling on waiting for a PVE task because a legitimate lock holder may be in such a wait the whole time

.PP
\fB--min-free-gib\fP=0
	minimum free GiB the storage must have (0 = $HARNESS_PROBE_MIN_FREE_GIB, else 520)

.PP
\fB--pool\fP="pveforge-harness"
	harness pool a VM must be a member of

.PP
\fB--roster\fP=""
	path to the roster file (overrides PVEFORGE_ROSTER and the default ./pveforge.toml)

.PP
\fB--static-only\fP[=false]
	run the static layer alone (no VM is created)

.PP
\fB--storage\fP=""
	the outer storage id (or $HARNESS_STORAGE)

.PP
\fB--tag\fP="pveforge-harness"
	harness tag a VM must carry


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpveforge-harness(1)\fP
